      <method name="set_translator_credits"
              c:identifier="gtk_about_dialog_set_translator_credits"
              glib:set-property="translator-credits"
              version="2.6">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtkaboutdialog.c"
             line="1686">Sets the translator credits string which is displayed in
the translators tab of the secondary credits dialog.

The intended use for this string is to display the translator
of the language which is currently used in the user interface.
Using gettext(), a simple way to achieve that is to mark the
string for translation:
|[&lt;!-- language="C" --&gt;
GtkWidget *about = gtk_about_dialog_new ();
gtk_about_dialog_set_translator_credits (GTK_ABOUT_DIALOG (about),
                                         _("translator-credits"));
]|
It is a good idea to use the customary msgid “translator-credits” for this
purpose, since translators will already know the purpose of that msgid, and
since #GtkAboutDialog will detect if “translator-credits” is untranslated
and hide the tab.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk/gtkaboutdialog.h" line="202"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <type name="none" c:type="void"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="about" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="gtk/gtkaboutdialog.c"
                 line="1688">a #GtkAboutDialog</doc>
            <type name="AboutDialog" c:type="GtkAboutDialog*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
          <parameter name="translator_credits"
                     transfer-ownership="none"
                     nullable="1"
                     allow-none="1">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="gtk/gtkaboutdialog.c"
                 line="1689">the translator credits</doc>
            <type name="utf8" c:type="const gchar*"/>
          </parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
