      <function name="get_for_display"
                c:identifier="gtk_clipboard_get_for_display"
                version="2.2">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtkclipboard.c"
             line="312">Returns the clipboard object for the given selection.
Cut/copy/paste menu items and keyboard shortcuts should use
the default clipboard, returned by passing %GDK_SELECTION_CLIPBOARD for @selection.
(%GDK_NONE is supported as a synonym for GDK_SELECTION_CLIPBOARD
for backwards compatibility reasons.)
The currently-selected object or text should be provided on the clipboard
identified by #GDK_SELECTION_PRIMARY. Cut/copy/paste menu items
conceptually copy the contents of the #GDK_SELECTION_PRIMARY clipboard
to the default clipboard, i.e. they copy the selection to what the
user sees as the clipboard.

(Passing #GDK_NONE is the same as using `gdk_atom_intern
("CLIPBOARD", FALSE)`.

See the
[FreeDesktop Clipboard Specification](http://www.freedesktop.org/Standards/clipboards-spec)
for a detailed discussion of the “CLIPBOARD” vs. “PRIMARY”
selections under the X window system. On Win32 the
#GDK_SELECTION_PRIMARY clipboard is essentially ignored.)

It’s possible to have arbitrary named clipboards; if you do invent
new clipboards, you should prefix the selection name with an
underscore (because the ICCCM requires that nonstandard atoms are
underscore-prefixed), and namespace it as well. For example,
if your application called “Foo” has a special-purpose
clipboard, you might call it “_FOO_SPECIAL_CLIPBOARD”.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk/gtkclipboard.h" line="187"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gtk/gtkclipboard.c"
               line="344">the appropriate clipboard object. If no
  clipboard already exists, a new one will be created. Once a clipboard
  object has been created, it is persistent and, since it is owned by
  GTK+, must not be freed or unrefd.</doc>
          <type name="Clipboard" c:type="GtkClipboard*"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <parameter name="display" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="gtk/gtkclipboard.c"
                 line="314">the #GdkDisplay for which the clipboard is to be retrieved or created.</doc>
            <type name="Gdk.Display" c:type="GdkDisplay*"/>
          </parameter>
          <parameter name="selection" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="gtk/gtkclipboard.c"
                 line="315">a #GdkAtom which identifies the clipboard to use.</doc>
            <type name="Gdk.Atom" c:type="GdkAtom"/>
