    <class name="ColorChooserWidget"
           c:symbol-prefix="color_chooser_widget"
           c:type="GtkColorChooserWidget"
           version="3.4"
           parent="Box"
           glib:type-name="GtkColorChooserWidget"
           glib:get-type="gtk_color_chooser_widget_get_type"
           glib:type-struct="ColorChooserWidgetClass">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gtk/gtkcolorchooserwidget.c"
           line="35">The #GtkColorChooserWidget widget lets the user select a
color. By default, the chooser presents a predefined palette
of colors, plus a small number of settable custom colors.
It is also possible to select a different color with the
single-color editor. To enter the single-color editing mode,
use the context menu of any color of the palette, or use the
'+' button to add a new custom color.

The chooser automatically remembers the last selection, as well
as custom colors.

To change the initially selected color, use gtk_color_chooser_set_rgba().
To get the selected color use gtk_color_chooser_get_rgba().

The #GtkColorChooserWidget is used in the #GtkColorChooserDialog
to provide a dialog for selecting colors.

# CSS names

GtkColorChooserWidget has a single CSS node with name colorchooser.</doc>
      <source-position filename="gtk/gtkcolorchooserwidget.h" line="67"/>
      <implements name="Atk.ImplementorIface"/>
      <implements name="Buildable"/>
      <implements name="ColorChooser"/>
      <implements name="Orientable"/>
      <constructor name="new"
                   c:identifier="gtk_color_chooser_widget_new"
                   version="3.4">
