      <method name="set_filter_func"
              c:identifier="gtk_list_box_set_filter_func"
              version="3.10">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtklistbox.c"
             line="1162">By setting a filter function on the @box one can decide dynamically which
of the rows to show. For instance, to implement a search function on a list that
filters the original list to only show the matching rows.

The @filter_func will be called for each row after the call, and it will
continue to be called each time a row changes (via gtk_list_box_row_changed()) or
when gtk_list_box_invalidate_filter() is called.

Note that using a filter function is incompatible with using a model
(see gtk_list_box_bind_model()).</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk/gtklistbox.h" line="275"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <type name="none" c:type="void"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
