      <method name="set_tab_detachable"
              c:identifier="gtk_notebook_set_tab_detachable"
              version="2.10">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtknotebook.c"
             line="7948">Sets whether the tab can be detached from @notebook to another
notebook or widget.

Note that 2 notebooks must share a common group identificator
(see gtk_notebook_set_group_name()) to allow automatic tabs
interchange between them.

If you want a widget to interact with a notebook through DnD
(i.e.: accept dragged tabs from it) it must be set as a drop
destination and accept the target “GTK_NOTEBOOK_TAB”. The notebook
will fill the selection with a GtkWidget** pointing to the child
widget that corresponds to the dropped tab.

Note that you should use gtk_notebook_detach_tab() instead
of gtk_container_remove() if you want to remove the tab from
the source notebook as part of accepting a drop. Otherwise,
the source notebook will think that the dragged tab was
removed from underneath the ongoing drag operation, and
will initiate a drag cancel animation.

|[&lt;!-- language="C" --&gt;
 static void
 on_drag_data_received (GtkWidget        *widget,
                        GdkDragContext   *context,
                        gint              x,
                        gint              y,
                        GtkSelectionData *data,
                        guint             info,
                        guint             time,
                        gpointer          user_data)
 {
   GtkWidget *notebook;
   GtkWidget **child;

   notebook = gtk_drag_get_source_widget (context);
   child = (void*) gtk_selection_data_get_data (data);

   // process_widget (*child);

   gtk_notebook_detach_tab (GTK_NOTEBOOK (notebook), *child);
 }
]|

If you want a notebook to accept drags from other widgets,
you will have to set your own DnD code to do it.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk/gtknotebook.h" line="281"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <type name="none" c:type="void"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
          <instance-parameter name="notebook" transfer-ownership="none">
            <doc xml:space="preserve"
                 filename="gtk/gtknotebook.c"
                 line="7950">a #GtkNotebook</doc>
            <type name="Notebook" c:type="GtkNotebook*"/>
          </instance-parameter>
