      <glib:signal name="get-child-position" when="last">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtkoverlay.c"
             line="807">The ::get-child-position signal is emitted to determine
the position and size of any overlay child widgets. A
handler for this signal should fill @allocation with
the desired position and size for @widget, relative to
the 'main' child of @overlay.

The default handler for this signal uses the @widget's
halign and valign properties to determine the position
and gives the widget its natural size (except that an
alignment of %GTK_ALIGN_FILL will cause the overlay to
be full-width/height). If the main child is a
#GtkScrolledWindow, the overlays are placed relative
to its contents.</doc>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gtk/gtkoverlay.c"
               line="828">%TRUE if the @allocation has been filled</doc>
          <type name="gboolean" c:type="gboolean"/>
        </return-value>
        <parameters>
