      <method name="join_group"
              c:identifier="gtk_radio_button_join_group"
              version="3.0">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtkradiobutton.c"
             line="370">Joins a #GtkRadioButton object to the group of another #GtkRadioButton object

Use this in language bindings instead of the gtk_radio_button_get_group()
and gtk_radio_button_set_group() methods

A common way to set up a group of radio buttons is the following:
|[&lt;!-- language="C" --&gt;
  GtkRadioButton *radio_button;
  GtkRadioButton *last_button;

  while (some_condition)
    {
       radio_button = gtk_radio_button_new (NULL);

       gtk_radio_button_join_group (radio_button, last_button);
       last_button = radio_button;
    }
]|</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk/gtkradiobutton.h" line="98"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <type name="none" c:type="void"/>
        </return-value>
