    <class name="StackSidebar"
           c:symbol-prefix="stack_sidebar"
           c:type="GtkStackSidebar"
           version="3.16"
           parent="Bin"
           glib:type-name="GtkStackSidebar"
           glib:get-type="gtk_stack_sidebar_get_type"
           glib:type-struct="StackSidebarClass">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gtk/gtkstacksidebar.c"
           line="34">A GtkStackSidebar enables you to quickly and easily provide a
consistent "sidebar" object for your user interface.

In order to use a GtkStackSidebar, you simply use a GtkStack to
organize your UI flow, and add the sidebar to your sidebar area. You
can use gtk_stack_sidebar_set_stack() to connect the #GtkStackSidebar
to the #GtkStack.

# CSS nodes

GtkStackSidebar has a single CSS node with name stacksidebar and
style class .sidebar.

When circumstances require it, GtkStackSidebar adds the
.needs-attention style class to the widgets representing the stack
pages.</doc>
      <source-position filename="gtk/gtkstacksidebar.h" line="59"/>
