      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gtk/gtktextchild.h"
           line="38">A #GtkTextChildAnchor is a spot in the buffer where child widgets can
be “anchored” (inserted inline, as if they were characters). The anchor
can have multiple widgets anchored, to allow for multiple views.</doc>
      <source-position filename="gtk/gtktextchild.h" line="72"/>
      <constructor name="new" c:identifier="gtk_text_child_anchor_new">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtktextchild.c"
             line="342">Creates a new #GtkTextChildAnchor. Usually you would then insert
it into a #GtkTextBuffer with gtk_text_buffer_insert_child_anchor().
To perform the creation and insertion in one step, use the
convenience function gtk_text_buffer_create_child_anchor().</doc>
