    <callback name="TreeIterCompareFunc" c:type="GtkTreeIterCompareFunc">
      <doc xml:space="preserve"
           filename="gtk/gtktreesortable.h"
           line="61">A GtkTreeIterCompareFunc should return a negative integer, zero, or a positive
integer if @a sorts before @b, @a sorts with @b, or @a sorts after @b
respectively. If two iters compare as equal, their order in the sorted model
is undefined. In order to ensure that the #GtkTreeSortable behaves as
expected, the GtkTreeIterCompareFunc must define a partial order on
the model, i.e. it must be reflexive, antisymmetric and transitive.

For example, if @model is a product catalogue, then a compare function
for the “price” column could be one which returns
`price_of(@a) - price_of(@b)`.</doc>
