      <method name="get_selected"
              c:identifier="gtk_tree_selection_get_selected">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtktreeselection.c"
             line="460">Sets @iter to the currently selected node, if @selection is set to
%GTK_SELECTION_SINGLE or %GTK_SELECTION_BROWSE.

The @iter argument may be %NULL if you just want to test if @selection
has any selected nodes.

The @model argument is filled with the current model as a convenience.

This function will not work with %GTK_SELECTION_MULTIPLE. See
gtk_tree_selection_get_selected_rows() instead.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk/gtktreeselection.h" line="130"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gtk/gtktreeselection.c"
