                   introspectable="0">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtktreestore.c"
             line="303">Creates a new tree store as with @n_columns columns each of the types passed
in.  Note that only types derived from standard GObject fundamental types
are supported.

As an example, `gtk_tree_store_new (3, G_TYPE_INT, G_TYPE_STRING,
GDK_TYPE_PIXBUF);` will create a new #GtkTreeStore with three columns, of type
#gint, #gchararray, and #GdkPixbuf respectively.</doc>
