      <method name="get_tooltip_context"
              c:identifier="gtk_tree_view_get_tooltip_context"
              version="2.12">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtktreeview.c"
             line="16386">This function is supposed to be used in a #GtkWidget::query-tooltip
signal handler for #GtkTreeView.  The @x, @y and @keyboard_tip values
which are received in the signal handler, should be passed to this
function without modification.

The return value indicates whether there is a tree view row at the given
coordinates (%TRUE) or not (%FALSE) for mouse tooltips.  For keyboard
tooltips the row returned will be the cursor row.  When %TRUE, then any of
@model, @path and @iter which have been provided will be set to point to
that row and the corresponding model.  @x and @y will always be converted
to be relative to @tree_view’s bin_window if @keyboard_tooltip is %FALSE.</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk/gtktreeview.h" line="584"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <doc xml:space="preserve"
               filename="gtk/gtktreeview.c"
               line="16409">whether or not the given tooltip context points to a row.</doc>
