                 line="2404">title of the window</doc>
            <type name="utf8" c:type="const gchar*"/>
          </parameter>
        </parameters>
      </method>
      <method name="set_titlebar"
              c:identifier="gtk_window_set_titlebar"
              version="3.10">
        <doc xml:space="preserve"
             filename="gtk/gtkwindow.c"
             line="4332">Sets a custom titlebar for @window.

A typical widget used here is #GtkHeaderBar, as it provides various features
expected of a titlebar while allowing the addition of child widgets to it.

If you set a custom titlebar, GTK+ will do its best to convince
the window manager not to put its own titlebar on the window.
Depending on the system, this function may not work for a window
that is already visible, so you set the titlebar before calling
gtk_widget_show().</doc>
        <source-position filename="gtk/gtkwindow.h" line="489"/>
        <return-value transfer-ownership="none">
          <type name="none" c:type="void"/>
        </return-value>
